      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "dac_bias_control",
        "description": "MCP4725 is a single-channel 12-bit I2C DAC powered from VCC_3V3. It receives commands from the MCU over the shared I2C bus and outputs an analog control voltage on VOUT. That VOUT is routed into the NE5532 channel-1 non-inverting input bias/control network, so the actual coupling, summing, or biasing implementation is completed by downstream passive circuitry. The A0 pin must be set to a defined logic state to select the intended I2C address; only one DAC instance is present, so no multi-device addressing is required beyond making the address deterministic.",
        "id": "dac_bias_control"
      },
