      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "audio_preamp",
        "description": "NE5532 implements the analog preamplifier stage from VIN_5V with common GND. Channel 1 is used as the active non-inverting amplifier path for the single audio channel; its non-inverting input network must accept the DAC-derived bias/control voltage while the remaining feedback and input signal conditioning are completed by downstream passive circuitry. The op-amp requires single-supply operation intent here, with VCC_P on VIN_5V and VCC_N on GND. Channel 2 is unused for signal processing; its IN2_P and IN2_N must be tied to a safe bias state and OUT2 left functionally unused to avoid floating unused amplifier inputs. This module exposes the DAC control-network entry and the amplified audio output port.",
        "id": "audio_preamp"
      },
